(320276,'2026-11-18T04:56:30','user679076639','ErrorHorror','THIS IS STARTING TO LOOK LIKE A DIGITAL APOCALYPSE.

What has happened over the past 8 days is hard to believe, and it keeps getting worse.

Nov 10: Apple''s iCloud and Apple ID went down worldwide, and people couldn''t even log in to their accounts.

Nov 12: Microsoft Outlook, Teams and Copilot crashed globally for over 24 hours, with 7.4 million outage reports.

Nov 13: Workday went down, and millions of workers couldn''t get into their pay or HR systems.

Nov 13: The FAA stopped every departing flight in America, and over 12,000 flights were cancelled that day.

Nov 16: JPMorgan''s systems failed, and it quickly spread to Bank of America, Wells Fargo and Zelle.

Nov 16: United Airlines'' whole system crashed, and planes couldn''t take off.

Nov 17: Charles Schwab''s website broke, and investors couldn''t log in.

Nov 17: Even the NSA''s classified communications network went down.

Nov 17: Now Apple Pay, iCloud, the App Store, Gmail, Google, Marriott and DoorDash are all having problems at the same time.

Nov 17: Equinor, Europe''s largest natural gas supplier, says it is under cyberattack.

Your bank, flights, email, payments, paycheck and America''s spy agency. All hit in one week.'),
